  "legend": {
    "gate.errors_now": "claim_gate.validate_claim errors of the claim exactly as drafted: the agent's to-do list",
    "gate.errors_if_proposals_accepted": "feasibility test only: the suggested candidates and placeholder text were put in a COPY of the claim; whatever still fails there has no machine evidence yet (compact form: clause_*_state x12 means twelve clauses)",
    "gate.only_judgment_left": "true when that copy passes the gate: every remaining gap is a judgment the agent makes from evidence already in the draft",
    "gate.placeholder_clause": "true when no clause inventory exists: the claim then holds one placeholder clause (DRAFT-PLACEHOLDER-no-clause-inventory) so the gate checks every part (an empty list makes the gate stop early, and the readiness tracker would count the unchecked steps); replace it with the real clauses",
    "proposals.later_source_search_machine": "complete machine searches, never put into the claim: copy the 'entry' of the same search_id from SUMMARY.json machine_searches into claim.later_source_search only after judging it adequate for the order and resolving every CONFLICT line",
    "readiness.by_step": "confirm = machine evidence is in the draft or proposals and an agent must check and accept it; agent_judgment = needs reading and a decision; resolve_conflicts = conflicts listed; research = no machine evidence yet; done_now / done_now_by_custody = the tracker already counts it; n/a = not applicable",
    "proposals": "candidates already in the claim's field shapes ('proposal'), with 'meta' explaining where each came from; dates are the acting instrument's signing or printed date, never a verified effective date (later-event proposals therefore say date_candidate; rename it to effective_date only after confirming)",
